      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galveston%2C_Indiana"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town hosts a branch of the Cass County Public Library, offering residents a quiet spot to dive into local history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galveston%2C_Indiana"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Nestled in Jackson Township, Cass County, Galveston sits about seven miles northwest of downtown Kokomo.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galveston%2C_Indiana"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Galveston was laid out in 1854, marking the beginning of a small Midwestern community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Galveston%2C_Indiana"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The town officially incorporated in 1870, solidifying its status on the Indiana map.",
